-- title:
--   The dirty-scratch word (round six, `word_dirty`)
-- statement:
--   **The dirty-scratch word.** `A` and `A'` are inverse on the scratch. Starting from any
--   scratch `s`, the word `L J L⁻¹ V L J L⁻¹ V` ends with scratch `s` and targets `y + B (A (C x))`.
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.R6BitNBWord`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem IntMul.Kappa.R6.Bit.word_dirty (hy : ∀ z : My, z + z = 0) (hs : ∀ z : Ms, z + z = 0)
--       (A A' : Ms →ₗ[R] Ms) (hA : ∀ z, A' (A z) = z) (B : Ms →ₗ[R] My) (C : Mx →ₗ[R] Ms)
--       (x : Mx) (y : My) (s : Ms) :
--       let s1 := A s
--       let y1 := y + B s1
--       let s2 := A' s1
--       let s3 := s2 + C x
--       let s4 := A s3
--       let y2 := y1 + B s4
--       let s5 := A' s4
--       let s6 := s5 + C x
--       s6 = s ∧ y2 = y + B (A (C x))
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** Round six, bit side: data-free scalar facts of the invocation word
--
--   The scalar part of one invocation (`L, J, L⁻¹, V, L, J, L⁻¹, V`, dirty scratch, characteristic
--   two) and the coefficient identity behind it, stated for any modules (in particular for the module
--   of formal frame values of `R6BitNBFormal`, where the two-stage motif needs them):
--
--   * `word_dirty`: with an invertible producer `A` on the scratch, an injection `B` (scratch →
--     targets) and a source copy `C` (inputs → scratch), the word restores **arbitrary** scratch and
--     adds `B (A (C x))` to the targets;
--   * `coeff_mod_two`: for triples `S, T`, `|S ∩ T| + [|S ∩ T| = 1] ≡ [S = T] (mod 2)`;
--   * `inject_identity`: if target `T` receives the retained point totals `star c` (`c ∈ T`) and the
--     excluded sums `star c \ (star t₁ ∪ star t₂)` (`T = {c, t₁, t₂}`), the total injected into `T`
--     is `x_T` (in characteristic two). This is the identity `M = I` of the scalar exchange.
